{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_coordination_lease_api_lease", "label": "Lease interface", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/coordination/lease-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The framework's distributed-lock abstraction: implementations differ in backing store, the contract is identical. Three working methods plus a callback registration, and an optional fifth for fencing tokens."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_coordination_lease_api_acquire", "label": "Lease.acquire", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/coordination/lease-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "false means 'another holder definitely has it'; a reject means 'I do not know'. Idempotent for a caller that already holds the lease."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_coordination_lease_api_acquirewithtoken", "label": "Lease.acquireWithToken", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/coordination/lease-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Optional, so consumers feature-detect and fall back to plain acquire() \u2014 which is exactly what LeaseMajority does. Both InMemoryLease and KubernetesLease implement it."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_coordination_lease_api_fencing_token", "label": "Fencing token", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/coordination/lease-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Lets an external observer order two acquires against the same lease; it rides on the coordination service's own optimistic-concurrency primitive (K8s resourceVersion, Redis SETNX with a counter, etcd revision). Opaque strings, compared exactly."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_coordination_lease_api_release", "label": "Lease.release", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/coordination/lease-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A no-op when not held, but it REJECTS when the backend was unreachable: a failed release leaves the record claimed on the server while this process has locally given it up, and not knowing whether you own the lease is information you need. Backends must propagate the error; cleanup-only callers wrap it. The flip side of the no-op: release does nothing while an acquire is still in flight, so an abandoned acquire cannot be undone until it reports back."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_coordination_lease_api_checkalive", "label": "Lease.checkAlive", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/coordination/lease-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A synchronous local check with no round trip, so it lags by up to one missed renewal \u2014 a sub-second window where the lease may already be gone while it still returns true. Use it to gate work, not as proof of ownership; for irrevocable actions take a backend round trip or rely on onLost."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_coordination_lease_api_onlost", "label": "Lease.onLost", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/coordination/lease-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fires once per loss; afterwards checkAlive() is false and acquire() is needed to regain ownership. The handler must drop ownership-dependent state at once and not wait on expensive work \u2014 the lease is gone and another holder may already be acting."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_coordination_lease_api_leasemajority", "label": "LeaseMajority", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/coordination/lease-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The split-brain strategy that feature-detects acquireWithToken and is the one caller that reacts to a release() rejection \u2014 it fails safe and stops claiming a majority until the partition heals."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_coordination_lease_api_custom_backend_requirements", "label": "Custom lease backend requirements", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/coordination/lease-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Three things every backend must get right: atomic acquire (the consistency model must produce exactly one winner), periodic renewal at roughly ttl/3, and accurate onLost including the TTL-expiry case. Test against concurrent acquires, a partition where both sides renew, holder crash plus re-acquire after TTL, and a holder pause (GC stall) longer than the TTL \u2014 a TTL-based lease cannot tell 'crashed' from 'paused'."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_coordination_lease_api_lease", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_coordination_lease_api_acquire", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/coordination/lease-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_coordination_lease_api_lease", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_coordination_lease_api_release", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/coordination/lease-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_coordination_lease_api_lease", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_coordination_lease_api_checkalive", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/coordination/lease-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_coordination_lease_api_lease", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_coordination_lease_api_onlost", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/coordination/lease-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_coordination_lease_api_acquirewithtoken", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_coordination_lease_api_acquire", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/coordination/lease-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_coordination_lease_api_acquirewithtoken", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_coordination_lease_api_fencing_token", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/coordination/lease-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_coordination_lease_api_leasemajority", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_coordination_lease_api_acquirewithtoken", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/coordination/lease-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_coordination_lease_api_leasemajority", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_coordination_lease_api_release", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/coordination/lease-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_coordination_lease_api_custom_backend_requirements", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_coordination_lease_api_lease", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/coordination/lease-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_coordination_lease_api_lease", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cluster_sharding_with_lease_coordinator_lease", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/coordination/lease-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_coordination_lease_api_checkalive", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cluster_sharding_introspection_partial_answer_deadline", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.65, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/coordination/lease-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}], "hyperedges": [{"id": "lease_contract_backends_and_consumers", "label": "Lease contract, its backends and its cluster consumers", "nodes": ["docs_src_content_docs_de_coordination_lease_api_lease", "docs_src_content_docs_de_coordination_in_memory_lease_inmemorylease", "docs_src_content_docs_de_coordination_kubernetes_lease_kuberneteslease", "docs_src_content_docs_de_cluster_sharding_with_lease_coordinator_lease", "docs_src_content_docs_de_cluster_singleton_with_lease_singleton_lease"], "relation": "participate_in", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/coordination/lease-api.mdx"}]}